# Scoped ignores, one line per file and rule. Everything not listed here is
# enforced, and the rule stays on for every role added later.
#
# roles/firewall: var-naming[no-role-prefix] fires on two deliberate parts of
# the role's public interface.
#
#   * `firewall` cannot be renamed. It is the variable
#     fedora.linux_system_roles.firewall itself reads, and this role hands its
#     generated configuration over in it.
#   * `common_firewall_*`, `group_firewall_*` and `host_firewall_*` are the
#     layering interface, and they are meant to be set in group_vars and
#     host_vars rather than on the role. Prefixing them `firewall_` would make
#     them look like role options, which is the opposite of what they are.
#
# Revisit with the firewall role cleanup effort.
roles/firewall/defaults/main.yml var-naming[no-role-prefix]
roles/firewall/tasks/layers.yml var-naming[no-role-prefix]
